{"id": "EUVD-2026-103727", "enisaUuid": "39004265-34dc-3516-b8fc-0ad070aeff04", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bridge: mdb: restart port group walk after deletion\n\nbr_mdb_flush_pgs() keeps a pointer-to-pointer cursor while walking\nmp->ports. br_multicast_del_pg() can re-enter the same MDB entry through\nbr_multicast_sg_del_exclude_ports() and unlink other port groups. If the\ncursor points into one of those groups, the next iteration dereferences a\nstale cursor and can leave mp->ports pointing at freed memory.\n\nA following RTM_GETMDB exposes the dangling pointer:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in br_mdb_dump\n  Read of size 8\n    br_mdb_dump\n    rtnl_mdb_dump\n    rtnl_dumpit\n    netlink_dump\n\nReset the cursor to mp->ports after every deletion. The deletion removes at\nleast the selected group, so the restarted walk always makes progress.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46ec55855c972504258c371677ac039ba20e5d12", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab3c4a4c85f2e1e8d04b5c1770dea8412d21c7fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe2a42789c12eb7c5d3a42191e2cc735a6c35ead", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab1404ac81154a89fb61ac50ae9a04cd8d4834dc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98487", "GHSA-vh4c-7r22-fq6w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "061501c8-9497-3733-acdb-1b7ede34d340", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "206939a9-b574-3609-b013-03a82f66f07c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6acb535afb2a3b688a7858f05b61f0433e480d5 <ab3c4a4c85f2e1e8d04b5c1770dea8412d21c7fe"}, {"id": "25c5031e-7c43-36cc-af07-cb073662dc01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "4a46be43-a799-3e1b-a627-0260c8f76f09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "5ebe7389-e087-3736-9709-a134e3fc2342", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "679d8cd8-1068-338f-992e-cf308495d5da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "77363e96-141f-3d51-a8f6-5a5f1151c67d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6acb535afb2a3b688a7858f05b61f0433e480d5 <ab1404ac81154a89fb61ac50ae9a04cd8d4834dc"}, {"id": "8d942d5e-a7b3-310c-a2fa-846c6dc77356", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a7f570a9-c75c-3e34-a0bd-7b1bd16358a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6acb535afb2a3b688a7858f05b61f0433e480d5 <fe2a42789c12eb7c5d3a42191e2cc735a6c35ead"}, {"id": "b05ca6c8-d484-3288-986b-7a1b45c1576b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6acb535afb2a3b688a7858f05b61f0433e480d5 <46ec55855c972504258c371677ac039ba20e5d12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dbfab86a-968c-392a-a557-b82be7eebb2f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}